/ locals: current_server, result
- content_for :title, "Player lookup"

= render "servers/container", current_server: do
  .mb-4
    h1.mb-1 Player lookup
    p.text-muted.mb-0 Find a player by Steam UID, Discord ID, or name.

  = render "servers/players/lookup", current_server:

  .card.border-secondary
    .card-body.text-center.py-5
      i.bi.bi-person-x.text-muted.fs-1.d-block.mb-3

      / Two different findings, not two flavours of failure. Which one it is tells an admin whether the player is
      / someone ESM has never met or someone it knows by Discord alone.
      - if result.unregistered?
        h5.text-light.mb-2 No Steam account linked
        p.text-muted.mb-2.mx-auto style="max-width: 34rem;"
          | ESM knows that Discord account, but nobody has ever linked a Steam account to it. Without one there's no Steam UID to look up, and no character on #{current_server.server_id} to find.
      - else
        h5.text-light.mb-2 No ESM account
        p.text-muted.mb-2.mx-auto style="max-width: 34rem;"
          | Nothing in ESM is using that Discord ID. They may still play on #{current_server.server_id}: ESM only learns who someone is once they've linked their Discord and Steam accounts.

      p.text-muted.small.mb-4
        | Looked up
        span.font-monospace.ms-1 = result.query

      = link_to server_players_path(current_server.public_id), class: "btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
        i.bi.bi-people.me-1
        | Search #{current_server.server_id} by name instead
